EXTRA QUESTIONS
Q: What is K-Means? How to choose K? A: Unsupervised clustering algorithm. K = number of clusters. Choose K using the Elbow plot, picking K where the inertia curve bends.
Q: What is TF-IDF? A: Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency. TF = how often a word appears in a doc. IDF = log(total docs / docs containing the word). Common words get low weight.
Q: Supervised vs unsupervised learning? A: Supervised uses labelled data (Naive Bayes, SVM). Unsupervised has no labels (K-Means, Hierarchical Clustering). Clustering is unsupervised.
Q: What is data normalization? A: Scaling features to a common range. Min-Max scales to [0,1]; Standard (Z-score) gives mean 0, std 1. Prevents large-valued features from dominating.
